---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import Callout from "../../components/Callout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";

const datasetsInstall = `conda create --name mrna_bench python=3.12
conda activate mrna_bench
python -m pip install mrna-bench`;

const paths = `import mrna_bench as mb

mb.update_data_path("/absolute/path/to/mrnabench-data")
mb.update_model_weights_path("/absolute/path/to/model-weights")`;

const sourceInstall = `python -m pip install \\
  --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu126 \\
  torch==2.7.1

python -m pip install wheel packaging ninja
python -m pip install --no-build-isolation 'mrna-bench[base_models]'`;

const loadDataset = `import mrna_bench as mb

dataset = mb.load_dataset("go-mf")

print(dataset.dataset_name)
print(dataset.data_df.shape)
print(dataset.metadata.task, dataset.metadata.default_split_type)`;

const firstBenchmark = `import torch
import mrna_bench as mb

from mrna_bench.embedder import DatasetEmbedder
from mrna_bench.linear_probe import LinearProbeBuilder

device = torch.device("cuda")

dataset = mb.load_dataset("go-mf")
model = mb.load_model(
    "Orthrus",
    "orthrus-large-6-track",
    device=device,
)

embeddings = DatasetEmbedder(
    model,
    dataset,
    batch_size=8,
).embed_dataset()
embeddings = torch.stack(embeddings).cpu().numpy()

probe = (
    LinearProbeBuilder(dataset)
    .fetch_embedding_by_embedding_instance(
        model.short_name,
        embeddings,
    )
    .build()
)

metrics = probe.run_linear_probe(random_seed=2541)
print(metrics)`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Quickstart"
  description="Install the package, choose its storage paths, load a dataset, and run one linear probe."
  section="Start"
>
  <h2>Install from PyPI</h2>
  <p>
    The base package includes dataset loading and evaluation. Install the model
    extra when you also need model inference.
  </p>

  <h3>Datasets and evaluation</h3>
  <CodeBlock code={datasetsInstall} language="shell" />

  <h3>Model inference</h3>
  <CodeBlock code={sourceInstall} language="shell" />

  <Callout tone="important" label="CUDA requirement">
    <p>
      The model extra builds <code>flash-attn</code> and
      <code>mamba-ssm</code> CUDA extensions from source. Use a CUDA 12.6
      development environment with matching headers and <code>nvcc</code>.
      Check the model catalog and checkpoint card for GPU, memory, attention
      backend, and track requirements.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h2>Set persistent storage</h2>
  <p>
    mRNABench downloads processed data and model weights outside the package.
    Set these paths once before loading a dataset or model. If the model path is
    omitted, it defaults to a <code>model_weights</code> directory below the
    data path.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={paths} language="python" />

  <h2>Load a dataset</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={loadDataset} language="python" />
  <p>
    A successful load prints <code>go-mf</code>, the dataframe dimensions, and
    metadata containing a multilabel task with a homology split.
  </p>

  <h2>Run one benchmark in memory</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={firstBenchmark} language="python" />
  <p>
    <code>LinearProbeBuilder</code> uses the first task and target in the
    dataset metadata, along with the dataset's default split. The benchmarking
    guide shows how to change those choices and save larger runs. The printed
    dictionary contains validation metrics with <code>val_</code> prefixes.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
